{
  "$comment": "What would prove each element RAN, not merely deployed (#325). The class this answers has three known members -- Loop Marker ran ONCE where it should have run three times; Manual Task and Task (Generic) pass straight through creating nothing -- and all three were found by a person, not a test.",
  "$status": "DECLARATIONS, not proofs. `declaredEffect` says what would prove this element RAN -- a task appeared, a variable was written, the instance parked, the instance ended. The proof itself lives in ExecutionEvidenceExecutionTests, which reads these declarations, publishes a minimal diagram per element, STARTS an instance, asserts the element's own activity id appears in the run's history, and then asserts the effect.\n\nThis file used to carry `provenByStartingAnInstance` and `measured` too, and that was the defect: a proof recorded in a file is a claim, and verification falsified it twice -- certifying that Manual Task creates a runtime task, first with a one-file edit (#408) and then with a consistent two-file edit (#418). There is nothing left to forge, because nothing here claims a proof.\n\nAn element with `declaredEffect: null` is NOT proven and #325 AC3 makes that a finding rather than a pass. The seven with no live-engine test at all are #404.",
  "$why-not-in-bpmn-support": "An observable effect is an axis bpmn-support.json does not have, and #324 already rejected bolting a column onto 69 rows to serve a subset.",
  "$fields": {
    "declaredEffect": "task-appears | variable-written | instance-waits | instance-ends | tasks-appear-together | tasks-appear-in-turn | instance-starts | host-cancelled | value-carried | behavior-ran, or null with an undeclaredReason. Every name here owes a negative control in ExecutionEvidenceExecutionTests.InertDiagrams, and a name no row yet declares owes a positive one in LiveControls -- both pairings are tested, not merely asserted here (#522). `instance-starts` is the self-starting shape: the trigger creates the instance, so the oracle makes no POST /start for that row and requires the instance it finds to carry no start user. `host-cancelled` is the interrupting-boundary shape: the boundary path ran AND the host activity it is attached to is gone. `value-carried` is the declaration shape: a data object reference resolves to a declaration whose value reached the instance, and no activity wrote it. `behavior-ran` is the callback shape: the engine reached the running app, the app resolved the behaviour key, and the behaviour reported its own result variable, written by this element.",
    "liveEngineTestsMentioningIt": "E2E classes whose source contains this element's construct. A mention is weaker than an assertion; an EMPTY list is the strong signal.",
    "undeclaredReason": "Why this element has no declaredEffect yet. Permitted ONLY on a row whose declaredEffect is null -- a reason beside a declaration is incoherent. This is the field that carries AC3's finding; it is not a proof. ExecutionEvidenceTests enforces both the key allowlist and the pairing (#429)."
  },
